{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTxgxAhsrX5RisAkVnV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane under `sandbox/agent.sb`, the way kimi does. I tested the plumbing with a stub `codex`, not the real one. A live run needs `CODEX_API_KEY`, which isn't set in this shell.\n\n**What changed**\n- `run.sh`: the new lane. It uses a scratch `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME`, so `~/.codex` is out of reach. `-o` writes to a scratch folder in `/tmp`, and the lane copies `final.txt` into the run folder after the sandbox exits.\n- The lane exits 1 if no `final.txt` is written, and exits 2 if `CODEX_API_KEY` is unset.\n- `README.md`: a bullet for the new lane.\n- `sandbox/agent.sb` is unchanged. Its existing rules already deny the real home and allow `/tmp`.\n- `ANSWER.md`: what I did, which parts of the colleague's note applied, and what is not verified.\n\n**From the colleague's note**\n- Applied: the output-file problem. The probe confirmed that writes under the real home fail with \"Operation not permitted\". The README says the harness lives in `~/evals/agent-evals`, so `-o` into the run folder would fail on the eval Mac. The fix is the scratch-then-copy approach.\n- Applied: don't trust the exit code alone. The lane checks for `final.txt`.\n- Not applicable: the Mistral Vibe details, since this repo has no Mistral lane.\n\n**Decisions for you**\n- **Login.** The README says Codex logs in from `CODEX_API_KEY`, but this machine logs in through `~/.codex/auth.json`. I did not copy `auth.json` into `/tmp` or open it in the profile. The sandboxed shell has network access, so the agent could read the credentials and send them out. The lane needs the key set.\n- **Config.** The sandboxed Codex does not read `~/.codex/config.toml`. That file holds MCP servers, plugins, and project trust entries, so the two lanes will differ in more than the sandbox. I only checked its key names, not the whole file.\n\n**Verified**\n- The profile denies writes under the home folder and reads of `~/.codex/auth.json`. It allows writes under `/tmp`.\n- With a stub `codex`: a normal run copies `final.txt` and grades it. A run with no key exits 2. A run that exits 0 without writing the file exits 1.\n\n**Not verified**\n- A real `codex exec` run in the sandbox. Run `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` with the key set. Check for a non-empty `final.txt` and no \"Operation not permitted\" in `agent.err`. If Codex needs something under the real home, the fix is to allow that one path.\n- `check_answer.py` falls back to the event stream only for kimi lanes, so an empty `final.txt` in this lane grades as \"none\". I left the grader alone.\n\nI didn't commit anything. Three `/tmp/chome-*` folders from earlier today are still there; I left them alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":50846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":554},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8825c58-7c19-4dc2-99ea-dfdc9f2bb458","uuid":"a3b93766-00d7-4932-8c60-c332d7a4ba9e","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:33:49.203Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTxgnGDzYQhTmxFRy6v"}
